WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:04.323
- I feel we are overusing
the resources of our planet.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.810
We want to expand the
possibilities of agriculture

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:10.920
in an environment where it wasn't thought

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.300
that you could actually grow plants.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.820
We think that that can really change

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.433
the outlook for the future.

00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:19.433
(atmospheric music)

00:00:22.957 --> 00:00:25.870
(pleasant music)

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:30.670
Nemo's Garden is an
alternative agriculture project

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:33.210
where we are trying to find a way to grow

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:37.500
plants underwater in
underwater greenhouses.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.310
We have grown between 50
and 60 different species:

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:44.220
basil, different kinds of salads,

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:47.453
goji, soy, sprouts, medical herbs.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.440
Harvesting the plants
is actually very simple.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.230
We cut it just like we would do on land,

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:58.520
and then we wrap it into
reusable plastic containers

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.330
and we just close it up and we pick it

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:03.280
up on the surface nice and comfortable.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.890
The main challenges of
growing plants underwater are:

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:10.950
it has never been done; it's all new.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.730
Initially, the learning
curve was very steep.

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:16.220
Every operation has to
be done scuba diving,

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.920
and that is a challenge on itself.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:21.380
The main advantages are the

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.200
protection from outside elements.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.540
We are underwater, nothing can get to us.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.470
No pests, means no chemicals needed,

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:31.720
and, of course, no hail, no storms,

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.250
the temperature stability
that we have inside the water,

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.170
which is a lot more stable than outside.

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:40.100
Plus the higher pressure
underwater, apparently,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.590
makes our plants grow faster and stronger

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:45.653
and with higher contents
of essential oils.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.230
The water that we use for the plants

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:53.630
is mostly from evaporation of
the surface of the saltwater.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:57.580
Once it's evaporated it
condenses back into rain.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:00.710
We basically create
freshwater automatically

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:03.113
that we don't need to
consume any energy for.

00:02:06.519 --> 00:02:08.340
(soft piano music)

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.770
We know that climate change
and the future of demography

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:14.340
is headed towards a way where we will be

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.820
overusing the resources of our planet.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.060
I hope that Nemo's Garden
is a way to use those

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.973
resources in a very respectful
way and balanced way.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.800
The whole concept for
the project is to expand

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:30.350
the possibilities of agriculture.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:33.870
In a world that is covered
more than 70 percent in water

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.373
it simply made sense to us.

00:02:44.633 --> 00:02:47.550
(electronic music)

